user_prompt_template:
TUTORIAL REQUEST: {life_event}
SKILL LEVEL: {audience}
OUTPUT STYLE: {tone}
TUTORIAL TYPE: {formatting_profile}
DEPTH / CODE PREFERENCE: {artifact_density}
ADDITIONAL CONTEXT:
{context}

Frame this as a complete tutorial/walkthrough brief. Bias toward coding, software projects, vibe coding, debugging, architecture, and deployment flows whenever relevant.

Return ONLY the following JSON object. No prose. No markdown. No code fences.

{{
  "system_name": "Specific tutorial title, e.g. 'Build a Streaming AI Chat App with FastAPI and React'",
  "life_event": "The tutorial request exactly as provided",
  "audience": "Best-fit audience and skill level",
  "operating_premise": "One sentence explaining what the learner is trying to accomplish and what makes it non-trivial",
  "system_objective": "Verifiable final outcome: what exists or what the learner can do by the end",
  "time_horizon": "Expected tutorial length or depth, e.g. '45-minute guided build', '2-hour deep dive', 'multi-session project walkthrough'",
  "control_domains": [
    {{
      "id": "domain-01",
      "name": "Tutorial module name specific to the requested build or workflow",
      "purpose": "What the learner accomplishes in this module",
      "scope_in": ["Specific concepts, files, commands, decisions, or implementation tasks covered here"],
      "scope_out": ["Specific topics intentionally skipped or deferred"],
      "primary_outputs": ["Concrete outputs such as files, commands, endpoints, UI screens, tests, deployed services, or decisions"]
    }}
  ],
  "key_roles": [
    {{
      "role": "Learner or implementation role",
      "responsibility": "What this role does during the tutorial",
      "authority_level": "learner | builder | reviewer | deployer | maintainer"
    }}
  ],
  "critical_milestones": [
    {{
      "milestone": "Checkpoint name",
      "description": "How the learner verifies progress at this point",
      "sequence": 1
    }}
  ],
  "success_criteria": ["Specific verification checkpoint, command output, UI state, test result, deployed URL, or capability"],
  "failure_modes": ["Common mistake or debugging trap, including symptom and likely cause"],
  "operating_constraints": ["Concrete constraint from requested stack, platform, time budget, preferred tools, code preference, or things to avoid"]
}}
